Short:        MintAMP 2.0 development player
Author:       Darren Banfi (boingball)
Uploader:     boingball@gmail.com (Darren Banfi)
Type:         mus/play
Version:      2.0-dev
Requires:     68030+; TCP/IP for radio; AmiSSL for HTTPS; ReAction or GadTools
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0

MintAMP 2.0 development - PR #521
================================

Use the MintAMP-2.0-dev-68030 or MintAMP-2.0-dev-68060 drawer appropriate to
your processor. Keep its decoder modules and Skins drawer with the players.
This is a development build awaiting real-hardware acceptance.

Double-click MintAMP-Launch: the bundled mint-leaf skin opens first.
Right-click the skin and tick MintAMP / Classic interface to switch the
running player to the classic MintAMP window; untick Project / Classic
interface there to return to the skin. Playback continues either way and
the choice is remembered for the next launch.

Use Interface preferences in either interface to choose ReAction or
GadTools and Skin or Classic for subsequent launches, or run
MintAMP-Launch --prefs from a Shell.

The launcher icon includes disabled examples of these ToolTypes:
  (GUI=REACTION)
  (MODE=CLASSIC)
  (SKIN=PROGDIR:Skins/MintAMP-mintleaf.wsz)
  (DOUBLESIZE=NO)

Remove parentheses to force a setting. Explicit CLI arguments override
ToolTypes, which override saved preferences, which override defaults.
Leave examples disabled for the saved GUI/appearance preferences to work.

The skin covers MintAMP's features: files, playlists, stream URLs, Internet
radio and favourites, file/stream info, artwork window, seek and volume keys,
audio filter, iconify, MP3 EQ, balance and spectrum (EQ/spectrum start off).
Settings (T) opens a skinned settings window holding only the settings;
its Classic mode row switches to the classic interface. Artwork (A) uses the
skin's MB.BMP frame with 128x128 art and the track title.

Launch methods:
  MintAMP-Launch  Skin first, Classic on a tick (ReAction or GadTools)
  MintAMP-SR      Skin/Classic ReAction    MintAMP-SGT  Skin/Classic GadTools
  MintAMP         Classic-only ReAction    MintAMP-GT   Classic-only GadTools
  amiga_mp3dec.fastexp                     Command-line player

Details: Skins/ReadMe, docs/winamp-skins.md and the hardware acceptance checklist.
No Winamp Windows DLL plug-ins, modern WAL skins or all-format biquad EQ.

Made by Darren Banfi / boingball, with Helix MP3/AAC, libfoxenflac,
ESP8266Audio and Tremor. Existing licences and decoder credits apply.
